# Video Agent

One prompt becomes a continuous 40-second story: four 10-second shots with enforced
narrative and visual continuity. This solves *continuity*, not generation — text-to-video
models already generate isolated clips fine; four clips from four prompts otherwise show a
protagonist whose face, room colour, and story never hold together across shots.

This is one of three products (Video Agent, Sales Agent, SQL Agent) on a shared Entermind
platform. This repo builds Video Agent only. Shared platform behaviour (harness, gateway,
orchestration, observability, failure handling) is specified once and referenced, not
re-implemented per feature — see `docs/architecture/platform-spec-summary.md`.

Full source documents: `docs/architecture/platform-spec-summary.md` (Entermind Common
Platform Specification v1.0) and `docs/architecture/video-agent-prd-summary.md`
(Video Agent PRD v1.0), both dated 2 Aug 2026. When this rule set is silent, those documents
govern. When they conflict with a request, say so before proceeding.
